message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Tech-Panic Tracker: two centuries of predictions about technology replacing human labour, classified and evaluated"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Jayes
    given-names: Jonathan
    email: jonathan.jayes@nexergroup.com
  - family-names: Schneider
    given-names: Ben
    email: benjamin.schneider@iakh.uio.no
    affiliation: "Department of Archaeology, Conservation and History (IAKH), University of Oslo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/j-jayes/tech-panic-tracker"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-08-03"
keywords:
  - technological unemployment
  - automation
  - forecasting evaluation
  - economic history
  - labour economics
  - open data
abstract: >-
  A systematic, preregistered, open dataset of predictions about technology
  replacing human labour, from the industrial revolution to the present,
  classified by level, technology generality, time horizon, mechanism, and
  author type, and evaluated against employment outcome data with a graded,
  evidence-cited rubric.
